        <mxCell id="notes" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;spacingRight=10;fillColor=#FAFAFA;strokeColor=#9E9E9E;" value="&lt;b&gt;Notes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;1. &lt;b&gt;Power:&lt;/b&gt; power bank USB-A → cut cable: red to the button&#39;s C contact, NO contact to the board&#39;s +5 V (VIN) screw terminal, black to the GND screw terminal. The button&#39;s LED + goes to the NO side (same point as VIN), LED − to GND, so it lights only when on. NC stays unconnected. Use one power input at a time (not USB-C and VIN together).&lt;br&gt;2. &lt;b&gt;PN532:&lt;/b&gt; SPI mode (DIP SW1 OFF, SW2 ON), 3V3 and GND from the board; SCK→GPIO12, MISO→GPIO13, MOSI→GPIO11, SS→GPIO10 on the Ethernet header. Keep magnets away from the reader.&lt;br&gt;3. &lt;b&gt;Speakers:&lt;/b&gt; the outputs are bridge-tied – connect each speaker between its own + and − terminal, never to GND." vertex="1">
